    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1226">

                <pb facs="0996" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2905.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-26T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Relative to the Ciudad Juárez situation and according to the information conveyed
                    in my February 26, 5 p.m., I have sent a friendly but firm note to Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
